% SCAFFOLDING stand-in for SIMPOS's class `temporary_window`, compiled by
% psi/espc.py into the package `simpos`.  It is NOT SIMPOS: the class body
% is lost (docs/simpos/subsystems/window.md §0.3, §1.2).  MENDELS (IFS
% No.61), 2026-11-27: the base class of its temporary_scroll and
% temporary_turn_menu (swindow.esp, win_class.esp), the library window's
% pop-up text windows (lib_win.esp:136-137); the last nature in 11 of 11
% held uses (window.md §1.2).
%
% THE MANUALS: TM-125 p6-7 (2.6 Temporary Window): it appears at the mouse
% cursor and disappears when the cursor goes out of it; it is taken off
% the screen, not hidden, when no longer needed; it is never hidden by an
% ordinary window; it saves the image it covers; p9 (4.2)
% as_temporary_window "the function as temporary window"; WINCS p5, p7-8
% (one of the three base classes).
% THE NATURE LIST IS INFERENCE, as inferior_window.esp's: the body is
% basic_window.esp's.  The attribute below puts a temporary window made
% with no position at the mouse when it is shown (TM-125 p6-7,
% basic_window.esp at_mouse/1); its frame pane saves what it covers and
% restores it when it is taken off (window_pane.esp, TM-125 p6-7).
% NOT STOOD IN: the disappearing when the mouse leaves (a temporary_menu
% does, temporary_menu.esp; for a temporary window no held run reaches
% it), never hidden by an ordinary window.

class temporary_window has

nature
        as_temporary_window,
        basic_window;

instance

% RECONSTRUCTED-FROM-MANUAL (TM-125 p6-7: it appears at the mouse cursor;
% the slot OURS)
attribute at_mouse := yes;

end.
